    "definitions": {
      "short": "to do or make (systematically and habitually), especially to practise",
      "usage": "commit, (evil-) do(-er), make(-r), ordain, work(-er).",
      "full": "H6466. paal מָּעַל 57 verb do, make (in poetry for עָשָׂה ) (Late Hebrew מּוֺעֵל workman , compare Jewish-Aramaic; Phoenician פעל = Biblical Hebrew (often); Arabic id. ; Old Aramaic; פעל ; Syriac in derived species and derivatives ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular Deut 32:27 +, אֵל פָ֫עַל Num 23:23 , 2 masculine singular מָּעַלְתָּ Exod 15:17 +, etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִפְעַל Job 22:17 +; 2 masculine singular תִּפְעָלֿ 35:6 , etc.; Infinitive construct לְפָעְָלָם 37:12 (see below); Participle active מֹּעֵל Psa 15:2 +, plural construct מֹּעֲלֵי 5:6 +, etc.; — 1 do: a. of God, with accusative (abstract) Num 23:23 ; Deut 32:27 ; Job 33:29 , יְשׁוּעוֺת Psa 74:12 ; + ל person 31:20 ; 68:29 ; Isa 26:12 ; Job 22:17 ; with accusative of congnate meaning with verb מֹּעַל Psa 44:2 ; Hab 1:5 ; accusative omitted Isa 43:13 , compare 41:4 . b. of men, with accusative Psa 11:3 ; Job 11:8 , + ל person (God) 7:20 , + ב person (God) 35:6 ; especially of doing evil, שָׁ֑קֶר Hosea 7:1 , עָוֶל Job 34:32 , עַוְלָה 36:23 ; Psa 58:3 ; 119:3 , אָוֶן Prov 30:20 , especially אָוֶן מֹּעֲלֵי Hosea 6:8 ; Isa 31:2 ; Job 31:3 ; 34:8 , 22 ; Psa 5:6 15t. in Psalms, Prov 10:29 ; 21:15 , רָע מֹּעֲלֵי Micah 2:1 ; rarely of doing right, with accusative מִשְׁמָּטוֺ Zeph 2:3 , צֶדֶק Psa 15:2 . c. of clouds, with accusative Job 37:12 (disregarding ֑֯ ). 2 make ; a. of God, with accusative concrete Exod 15:17 ; + ל of thing Prov 16:4 , ל of 2nd object Psa 7:16 ; מֹּעֲלִי Job 36:3 my Maker. b. of man, with accusative concrete Isa 44:12 , 15 ; accusative omitted 44:12 ; Psa 7:16 . &#8212; Isa 1:31 see מֹּעַל .",
      "rootNote": "a primitive root;",
